.TITLE "chown"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the owner and group of a file or directory. It is used to manage __administrative ownership__ of filesystem objects.

.DIV "TLDR"
**chown user file.txt**
Changes the owner of a file to a specific user.
> __user__ the new owner | __file.txt__ target file

**chown user:group file.txt**
Changes both the owner and the primary group of a file.
> __user__ new owner | __group__ new group | __file.txt__ target file

**chown -R user:group directory/**
Changes the owner and group for a directory and all its contents recursively.
> __-R__ recursive flag | __user:group__ new ownership | __directory/__ target folder

**chown -v user file.txt**
Displays a message for each file whose ownership is changed.
> __-v__ verbose flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, you typically need to use `**sudo**` with __chown__ to change ownership of files that you do not already own.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:chmod** **mac:ls**

